WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Illuminat...

3
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Illumination!

4
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.000
The year was 1985,

5
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.000
and the number one
show on TV was...

6
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Evil Bratt!

7
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.000
The show starred young
Balthazar Bratt as a child prodigy

8
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.000
and criminal mastermind
bent on world domination.

9
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.000
There he is! Get him!

10
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.000
I've been a bad boy!

11
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Bratt was the biggest
child actor of the 1980s,

12
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.000
striking a chord with
audiences all over the world.

13
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.000
There he is! Get him!

14
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.000
But it all came
to an end in Season 3, when...

15
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.000
I've been a bad boy!

16
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.000
The young star experienced
an unexpected growth spurt.

17
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Boy? Ugh!

18
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.000
The show was canceled.
Hollywood rejected him

19
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.000
and Bratt quickly plunged
into a downward spiral,

20
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.000
starting to actually believe he was
the character he played on TV.

21
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.000
What are you looking at?

22
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Leading us all to wonder,

23
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
where is he now?

24
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.000
You know what, Clive?

25
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.000
Playing a villain on TV was fun,

26
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.000
but being one in real life
is even better.

27
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Heist music!

28
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Here it comes.

29
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.000
What?
Clive, what are you doing?

30
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.000
How is that heist music?

31
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Sorry. My bad.

32
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Ew!

33
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.000
Mommy!

34
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.000
Stop or I'll...

35
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Sir, the ship has been boarded
by some kind of monster!

36
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Wait! That's not
a monster.

37
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.000
That's a man
wearing shoulder pads!

38
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.000
There's only one supervillain

39
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.000
whose fashion sense
is quite that dated.

40
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.000
Balthazar Bratt.

41
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.000
Blast it! The Dumont
Diamond is on that ship.

42
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:30.000
I want every agent in the area
on the scene immediately!

43
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.000
We're already here. Agents
Grucy are closing fast.

44
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.000
Yes! Wait.
What did you call us?

45
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.000
"Grucy." You know, GRU and
Lucy mushed together. Try it.

46
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.000
Oh! I like it,
but not a lot.

47
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.000
I don't like it.

48
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.000
Stop!
On the ground!

49
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.000
Go, go, go!

50
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.000
Eh?

51
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.000
Too late again, GRU!

52
00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.000
Wha?

53
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.000
He's getting away!

54
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.000
That's what he thinks.

55
00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.000
Go! Go! Go...

56
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.000
Go! Go! Go!
Go! Go!

57
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.000
I don't think we
can make it, GRU!

58
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.000
We can make it!

59
00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.000
We can make it!

60
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.000
No, we can't!

61
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.000
Ahh!

62
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.000
Get ready!

63
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.000
Get ready for...

64
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.000
Hey. How you doing?

65
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.000
Are you okay?

66
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.000
You guys are so cute.

67
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Go get him, GRU-GRU!

68
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.000
Hello, GRU.

69
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.000
How's your transition coming?

70
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.000
You know, from world's
worst villain

71
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.000
to world's worst agent?

72
00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.000
Oh, that's hilarious.
You should be on TV.

73
00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:59.000
Oh, that's right. You were!
But then you got canceled!

74
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.000
Ha-ha!

75
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.000
What about that?
Ugh!

76
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.000
What? Oh, girls!
Oh!

77
00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.000
Dance fight!

78
00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.000
Ow!

79
00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:32.000
Alpha Team, the diamond is secure.
Come and pick up the package.

80
00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.000
Copy that.
Alpha Team in approach.

81
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.000
GRU!

82
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Did you actually
think I was unconscious?

83
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Huh! It's called acting, hoser.

84
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.000
And clearly, I've still got it!

85
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.000
I've been a bad boy!

86
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.000
Freeze! Don't move!

87
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.000
Son of a Betamax!

88
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.000
Go, go! Get him!

89
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.000
He's getting away!

90
00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.000
This isn't over, GRU.

91
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.000
You hear me?
This is not over.

92
00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:23.000
Yeah? Well,
I still have the diamond.

93
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.000
Happy birthday to you

94
00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.000
Happy birthday to...

95
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:34.000
Happy birthday, dear Dan

96
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:40.000
Happy birthday to you

97
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.000
I can't believe
Bratt got away again.

98
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.000
How is this
possible? How?

99
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.000
And it's not just
that he got away,

100
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.000
it is he's so smug about it.

101
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:29.000
"Ooh, I've been
a bad boy!"

102
00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:33.000
Gah! Edna, hey!
Looking hot today.

103
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.000
Got cats on you.

104
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:40.000
And it was so humiliating, dangling
there in the bubble-gum Speedo.

105
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.000
And I didn't have time to
go to the gym this week,

106
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:48.000
and I had a big breakfast. And
was feeling a little bloated.

107
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.000
You know what? He's not
even worth talking about.

108
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:56.000
I don't even want to waste
another breath about the guy.

109
00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.000
And another thing!

110
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:04.000
Next time I see Bratt, I will
moonwalk all over his stupid face!

111
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.000
Thank you all for coming
at such short notice.

112
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:17.000
It is with great sadness that I
inform you that, as of today,

113
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:21.000
I am retiring as
head of the AVL.

114
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.000
Oh, no!

115
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:29.000
Your new leader is coming
directly from head office.

116
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.000
Effective immediately.

117
00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.000
She is the very gifted,

118
00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:40.000
very ambitious,
Miss Valerie da Vinci.

119
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:43.000
As I look out
over all your faces,

120
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.000
I am flooded with
so many memories.

121
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.000
Oh, boy!
This is a snooze fest!

122
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.000
Excuse me, this is my last...

123
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.000
Blah, blah, blah!
We understand.

124
00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:53.000
You're old, you're
fat, you're done.

125
00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.000
Let me breathe in.

126
00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.000
Ooh, broke a little sweat,
there.

127
00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.000
First order of business,

128
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:05.000
which one of you losers
is Agent GRU?

129
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.000
Oh, that would be me.

130
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.000
Although, I don't know if
I'd say "loser," per se.

131
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.000
Kind of is...

132
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.000
Oh, it's the girls!

133
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.000
Not a good time.

134
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.000
Hey!
Ahh!

135
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.000
Yes, sir!
Uh...

136
00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.000
Ma'am? You're making me nervous.

137
00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:29.000
How could you let
Balthazar Bratt,

138
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:31.000
the AVL's most wanted villain,

139
00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.000
just get away?

140
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.000
That is the opposite
of what we do here!

141
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.000
Okay, okay.

142
00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.000
Yes, maybe
he got away. Again.

143
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:42.000
But he didn't get the diamond.

144
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.000
And I am this close
to bringing him in.

145
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.000
This close.

146
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.000
Huh. Interesting.

147
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.000
You're fired!

148
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.000
What?

149
00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:54.000
That's totally not fair.
GRU is a great agent!

150
00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.000
You know what?
If you fire him,

151
00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.000
you're gonna have to
fire me, sister-sister.

152
00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.000
And do you really wanna do that?

153
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.000
Do ya?

154
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:05.000
No, no, no!

155
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.000
Well, I guess she did.

156
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.000
Honey, you didn't
have to do that.

157
00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:21.000
I know how much
you love your job.

158
00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:24.000
Well, I love other things more.

159
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.000
You know, we're gonna
have to tell the girls.

160
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.000
Can you do it?

161
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.000
The whole "mom" thing
is still kind of new to me.

162
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.000
Oh, sure.

163
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Huh?

164
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.000
Psst!

165
00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.000
Hello?

166
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:04.000
Aloha!

167
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.000
Oh!

168
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.000
This is unexpected.

169
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:11.000
Well, you never got to
go on a honeymoon, so...

170
00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.000
We made you dinner!

171
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.000
It's a luau!

172
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.000
We got pineapples and
coconuts and ukuleles!

173
00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.000
Oh! Yay!
Yay!

174
00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:34.000
The soup of the day.

175
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.000
Madame and Monsieur.

176
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.000
The gummy bears were my idea.

177
00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:46.000
Mmm! Looks too good
to even eat.

178
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.000
Am I right?

179
00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:51.000
But I made it for you. Oh.

180
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.000
Mmm-mmm-mmm!

181
00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:58.000
Good soup!
I love the combination

182
00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.000
of gummy bears

183
00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.000
and meat.

184
00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.000
I'm gonna hold it in my mouth.

185
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.000
'Cause it's so good, I
don't wanna swallow it.

186
00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:12.000
So, how was work?

187
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:16.000
Ooh, did you take that guy down?
Did anything explode?

188
00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.000
Well, actually,

189
00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:23.000
today, Lucy and I were
invited to not work

190
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.000
at the AVL anymore.

191
00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.000
No!

192
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.000
You got fired?

193
00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:34.000
Oh, no!
No, no, no.

194
00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.000
Yes.

195
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.000
But don't worry.

196
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:41.000
I'm sure we'll get
new jobs. Real soon.

197
00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.000
Even better ones.

198
00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:47.000
What's better than being
super-cool secret agents?

199
00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.000
Ooh, I know!
You could gamble online!

200
00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:52.000
That's what Katie's dad does.

201
00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:55.000
Okay. We will definitely
look into that.

202
00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.000
That's a good suggestion.

203
00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:02.000
And let's not go over
to Katie's house anymore.

204
00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.000
Hmm?

205
00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.000
Guys! Shh! I don't think
you heard me right.

206
00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:11.000
No, no, no.

207
00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:15.000
This does not mean that we are
going back to being villains.

208
00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:20.000
Okay, all right.
I get it.

209
00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.000
Look, I know it's been
a little tough lately.

210
00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:28.000
Especially with Dr. Nefario accidentally
freezing himself in carbonite.

211
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:35.000
But our life of crime is over!

212
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:39.000
Mel! Mel, you're
with me on this, right?

213
00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:01.000
Guys, listen to me!
Read my lips!

214
00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:09.000
What? What?

215
00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:12.000
Oh... What did I say?
It's not "comquit"?

216
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:14.000
Ah, okay.

217
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:18.000
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

218
00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:23.000
Don't take that tone with me!
We're not going back to villainy.

219
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:27.000
Yes! And I don't want to
hear another word about it.

220
00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:36.000
Look, if you guys don't stop right
now, there will be consequences.

221
00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:40.000
Hey! Don't say anything
you're going to regret.

222
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.000
What? You quit?

223
00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:50.000
You're serious?
Come on!

224
00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:57.000
Dave! Jerry!

225
00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:01.000
Great news, guys.
You have been promoted.

226
00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:05.000
You're in charge now.
Huh? Not bad.

227
00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:15.000
Jeesh!

228
00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.000
Ah, Monsieur Pompeux!

229
00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:39.000
To what do we owe the presence

230
00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:42.000
of the world's
foremost gem expert?

231
00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.000
The chief of police sent me.

232
00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:47.000
He was concerned that during
the recent heist attempt,

233
00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:51.000
the Dumont Diamond
was replaced with a phony.

234
00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.000
Ooh, la-la!

235
00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.000
You have been duped!

236
00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.000
What? We have?

237
00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:15.000
Yes.

238
00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.000
By me!

239
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:22.000
But, what is...

240
00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.000
Oh, no! Help!

241
00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:44.000
Ooh!

242
00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:48.000
I've been a bad boy!

243
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.000
Or should I say...

244
00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:09.000
Oh!

245
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.000
Hey, GRU.

246
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.000
What you doing down here?

247
00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.000
In the dark. Alone.

248
00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:40.000
Oh, nothing.
Just thinking.

249
00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.000
You okay?

250
00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:44.000
Oh, yes. Yeah, I'm fine.
I'm fine.

251
00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.000
It's just...

252
00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:50.000
I don't know.
I guess I just feel like

253
00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.000
a failure.

254
00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.000
Like I don't have
a purpose anymore.

255
00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:58.000
Hey, mister,
you are not a failure.

256
00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:01.000
If only I could
have nailed Bratt.

257
00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.000
So many times, I almost had him.

258
00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.000
But now I'll never
get the chance,

259
00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:09.000
'cause I have been
kicked to the curb.

260
00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:11.000
GRU, you've got to let this go.

261
00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.000
It's time to look forward.

262
00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.000
Things will get
better. I promise.

263
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.000
Excuse me.

264
00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:43.000
Pardon me, young people?

265
00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:46.000
Would you tell me
how to get to this address?

266
00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.000
I'm looking for a Mr. GRU.

267
00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:07.000
Idiots.

268
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.000
No! Kyle!

269
00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:14.000
Stop! Kyle, let go!

270
00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:19.000
No! No!

271
00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.000
You've got to be kidding me!

272
00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:22.000
Lucy, did you...

273
00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.000
He helps you if
you have nightmares.

274
00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.000
And he's really
good to snuggle with.

275
00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.000
Oh, no, no, no.
Agnes! Agnes!

276
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:30.000
So take good care of him.

277
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.000
Thank you!

278
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.000
Agnes, what are you doing?

279
00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.000
You sold your unicorn?

280
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:41.000
Well, I just wanted to help,
since you don't have a job.

281
00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.000
I got two whole dollars for it.

282
00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:48.000
Uh, excuse me?

283
00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.000
Sorry, buddy, the sale's over.

284
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:51.000
Yes, but this will
only take a...

285
00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:54.000
Hey, eyebrows, get off the lawn.

286
00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:55.000
Yeah, but...

287
00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:57.000
Hey, could you...

288
00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.000
Oh, uh, of course.

289
00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:01.000
Now, as I was saying, I...

290
00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:02.000
Uh... Oh.

291
00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:05.000
Goodbye!

292
00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:13.000
Listen, Agnes, you don't need to worry.
We're going to be fine.

293
00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.000
For real?

294
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.000
For real.

295
00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.000
Now, come on, let's
pack this stuff up.

296
00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.000
Ow! Ow!
Seriously?

297
00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:22.000
Buddy, you're not
getting the hint.

298
00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:25.000
Excuse me, Mr. GRU,

299
00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:28.000
but I really must
have a word with you.

300
00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.000
How do you know my name?

301
00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:34.000
Allow me to introduce myself.
My name is Fritz.

302
00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.000
Ow!

303
00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.000
Good puppy.

304
00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:41.000
And I am inquiring on behalf
of your twin brother, Dru.

305
00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:43.000
He needs your help.

306
00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:45.000
What? Twin brother?

307
00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:47.000
Twin brother?

308
00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:48.000
Oh, Ja.

309
00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:51.000
He would like to fly you
to Freedonia to meet him.

310
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:54.000
Your father has recently
passed away and...

311
00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:56.000
Okay, cuckoo.

312
00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:59.000
I'm sorry, but my dad
died when I was a baby,

313
00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.000
and I don't have any brother.
You got the wrong guy.

314
00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:08.000
Really? Well, then,
how do you explain this?

315
00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:17.000
Bellissimo!

316
00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.000
Oh, hello, GRU.

317
00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:22.000
Hi, Mom.

318
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:25.000
It's important to keep active
in one's golden years.

319
00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:27.000
Oh!

320
00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:30.000
There you are, you cutie, you.

321
00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.000
Oh!

322
00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:36.000
Uh, these are my
diving instructors.

323
00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:40.000
Vincenzo und Paolo.

324
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:42.000
Ciao, boys.

325
00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:44.000
So, what do you want?

326
00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:47.000
Mom, do I have a twin brother?

327
00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:51.000
Ah! How did you find out?
Who told you?

328
00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:52.000
Wait, what? It's true?

329
00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:54.000
You never told me
I had a brother!

330
00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:58.000
And you told me that Dad died of
disappointment when I was born.

331
00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:01.000
Ja, Ja.
That was the agreement.

332
00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:05.000
Agreement?
What are you talking about?

333
00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:10.000
Shortly after you and
your brother were born,

334
00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:13.000
your father and I divorced.

335
00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:16.000
We each took one son
to raise on our own

336
00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:21.000
and promised never to
see each other again.

337
00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:23.000
Obviously,

338
00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:26.000
I got second pick.

339
00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:31.000
I have a brother!

340
00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:40.000
Hey, girls! How are
things in Row B, huh?

341
00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:42.000
I put together some fun
activities for the trip!

342
00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:45.000
Who is up for some gin rummy?

343
00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:48.000
Yeah, um...

344
00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:49.000
We're good.

345
00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:51.000
Oh, okay.

346
00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:54.000
I'll just sit here
and play solitaire.

347
00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:56.000
I hope I win.

348
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:59.000
I wonder what Dru
will be like. Ooh!

349
00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:01.000
Maybe we'll have the twin thing

350
00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:04.000
when you can read
each other's minds, no?

351
00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.000
How cool would that be?

352
00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:08.000
Um, super cool!

353
00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:19.000
Ooh!

354
00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:29.000
Freedonia!
Freedonia! Freedonia!

355
00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:31.000
Hi, piggy, piggy!

356
00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:34.000
Whoa!
Look at that house!

357
00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:36.000
It's like a castle!

358
00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:40.000
I can't wait to meet my brother!

359
00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
Ugh. What's with
all the pigs?

360
00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:45.000
This is the family business.

361
00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:49.000
The largest pig farm in
the whole of Freedonia.

362
00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:52.000
Okay, nice pig.

363
00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:55.000
No! That's my
private part!

364
00:24:57.000 --> 00:25:00.000
This pig has issues!

365
00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:03.000
Please, come in.

366
00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:14.000
Oh, this is amazing!

367
00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:19.000
Ah, it's like the Sistine Chapel!
But with pigs.

368
00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:27.000
My brother!

369
00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.000
My brother!

370
00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:33.000
GRU!

371
00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:35.000
Dru!

372
00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:43.000
Oh!

373
00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:47.000
Brother! I am hugging you!

374
00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:49.000
I'm so happy!

375
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:53.000
After all of these years,
finally I'm meeting you!

376
00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:55.000
Yup. All right.
Good.

377
00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:57.000
Oh, look at that.

378
00:25:57.000 --> 00:26:00.000
You must be the beautiful wife.

379
00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:01.000
Beautiful?
Oh!

380
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:04.000
Stop it.
Sweet talker.

381
00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:06.000
How is my brother
finding a wife like you

382
00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:07.000
when he is so bald?

383
00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:10.000
I'm joking!

384
00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:15.000
These must be my nieces!

385
00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:19.000
You're Agnes! You
are small with big eyes.

386
00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:21.000
And it makes me wanna
put you into my pocket.

387
00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:23.000
You can't do that!

388
00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:25.000
I'm too big.

389
00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:29.000
Edith! I can tell that you
are a little mischievous.

390
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:32.000
We're gonna have to make
a little trouble later.

391
00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:34.000
I already have!

392
00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:37.000
Ow! Ow! Please!

393
00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:39.000
Why are you
doing that? Ow!

394
00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:43.000
Fist bump for
mischievous behavior!

395
00:26:43.000 --> 00:26:46.000
And Margo.
Oh, you are so mature!

396
00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:49.000
I'm guessing...
Mmm... 15?

397
00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:50.000
15?

398
00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:54.000
She's 12. She looks 12
and will always be 12.

399
00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:57.000
So, Dru, this place is amazing!

400
00:26:57.000 --> 00:27:00.000
I mean, you just walk through
the doors and you're like...

401
00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:03.000
Oh, it's nice, I guess, sure.

402
00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:06.000
I'm not really into things.

403
00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:11.000
- This is so cool!
- Look at that!

404
00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:13.000
Oh, my gosh!
He's even got a helicopter!

405
00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:15.000
This is the best!

406
00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:17.000
Yes, the best!

407
00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:19.000
All right, let's go home now.

408
00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.000
Home? Why?

409
00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:24.000
I don't know. This guy with
the mansion and the cars

410
00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:28.000
and all of the hair, with the
silky smooth, luxurious hair.

411
00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:31.000
I feel worse than
I did before I came.

412
00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:34.000
But he's your brother, GRU.
Give this a chance.

413
00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:35.000
Oh, I was thinking,
while GRU and I

414
00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:37.000
catch up on some brother stuff,

415
00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:40.000
you girls should go with Fritz.
He has a surprise for you!

416
00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:42.000
Yay!
Awesome!

417
00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:43.000
I love surprises!

418
00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:45.000
Oh, this is perfect!
Mother-daughter bonding time.

419
00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:47.000
Let's do it!
Woot-woot!

420
00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:50.000
Bye! You boys
have fun!

421
00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:53.000
Whoopi!

422
00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:58.000
Now you can be as
evil as Balthazar Bratt

423
00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:00.000
with the Evil Bratt
action figure.

424
00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.000
Featuring music-activated
breakdance mode.

425
00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:08.000
Also featuring bubblegum-launching
shoulder pads!

426
00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:13.000
And the all-new
Mega Diamond Laser!

427
00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:15.000
No more math!

428
00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:19.000
I've been a bad boy!

429
00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:22.000
The Mega Diamond Laser
does not actually incinerate books.

430
00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:25.000
How could
Hollywood cancel a show

431
00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:28.000
that produced toys
like this, Clive?

432
00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:31.000
Evil Bratt was a masterpiece!

433
00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:33.000
Does no one value
true art anymore?

434
00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:36.000
It's a disgrace
and a travesty, sir.

435
00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:39.000
Well, now that I've got the
diamond, it's payback time.

436
00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:43.000
Oh, it's too bad GRU won't be
around to try and stop me.

437
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:46.000
Oh, wait! No, it's not.
I hate that dweeb!

438
00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:48.000
And you, Hollywood!

439
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:51.000
This time, I'm canceling you

440
00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:55.000
and all the losers
who rejected me!

441
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.000
Oh, piggy, piggy!

442
00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:05.000
So, how are things going
for you career-wise?

443
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:08.000
Great!
So, so great!

444
00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:10.000
Crushing it.

445
00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:12.000
Well, I've got
something that I think

446
00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:16.000
you will find very interesting.

447
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Hold onto your face, brother.

448
00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:30.000
Yee-haw!
Yah, yah!

449
00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:41.000
Ow!

450
00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:52.000
Come on!
Come on!

451
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:56.000
What is all this?

452
00:29:56.000 --> 00:30:02.000
The pig farm was just a cover
for the real family business.

453
00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:11.000
Now, feast your eyes on

454
00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:14.000
Dad's lair!

455
00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:16.000
Ta-da!

456
00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:19.000
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait.

457
00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:22.000
So, our dad was a villain?

458
00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:24.000
No, no, no, not just a villain.

459
00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:28.000
One of the greatest of all time!

460
00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:32.000
He was known as the Bald Terror!

461
00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:36.000
That's him? Our dad?

462
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:39.000
He was so proud of you. And
what a great villain you were.

463
00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:41.000
He was?

464
00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:44.000
But me, eh, not so much.

465
00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:50.000
To Dad, I was just a failure.

466
00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:53.000
He never thought I had what
it took to be a villain.

467
00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:57.000
But now, you can help
me prove him wrong!

468
00:30:57.000 --> 00:30:59.000
Brother,

469
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:02.000
teach me the art of villainy!

470
00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:05.000
No.

471
00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:07.000
No, no, no.
I can't do that.

472
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:09.000
What? But
it's our family tradition!

473
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:12.000
You can't say no to that!

474
00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:13.000
Look, I'm sorry.

475
00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:17.000
I left that life behind me.
End of story.

476
00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:19.000
Oh.

477
00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:21.000
Okay. I understand.

478
00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:24.000
Hmm! I wonder
what this does.

479
00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:42.000
Holy Moley!

480
00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:44.000
Dad's villain wheels!

481
00:31:44.000 --> 00:31:47.000
Pretty slick, huh?

482
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:51.000
Hey, you wanna take her out for a spin?
Just for some fun?

483
00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:55.000
Mmm!

484
00:31:59.000 --> 00:32:02.000
Oh, oh, oh! Look out!

485
00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:06.000
What a beautiful day!

486
00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:09.000
Zero to 400 in three seconds.

487
00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:11.000
Able to withstand
a nuclear blast.

488
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:13.000
Armed to the teeth.

489
00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:17.000
Okay, that's pretty nice.

490
00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:20.000
And it's a hybrid.
Look out!

491
00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:44.000
Help me!

492
00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:50.000
I am not enjoying this.

493
00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:01.000
Whoa! What is
going on here?

494
00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:05.000
Welcome to the annual
Freedonian Cheese Festival.

495
00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:07.000
Go!

496
00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:14.000
Look, look!
Look at all the candies!

497
00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:17.000
Whoa!
Eep, eep, eep!

498
00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:20.000
Lucy, can we get these? Please.

499
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:23.000
Okay, but only
one each. I mean it.

500
00:33:23.000 --> 00:33:25.000
Aw!
Oh, man!

501
00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:28.000
No, I don't. Get as
many as you want. I don't care.

502
00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:30.000
Yay! Awesome!

503
00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.000
Uh...
What?

504
00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:35.000
Well, it's okay to tell them
no sometimes, too, you know?

505
00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:37.000
Moms need to be tough.

506
00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:39.000
Right, right.
Tough. Good one.

507
00:33:39.000 --> 00:33:40.000
I can totally do that.

508
00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:42.000
You know, still figuring
out this mom thing.

509
00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:45.000
Gettin' my sea legs, matey!

510
00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:48.000
It's a unicorn!

511
00:33:52.000 --> 00:33:55.000
Can we go in there?
Please, please, please!

512
00:33:57.000 --> 00:34:00.000
Um... Sure! Yeah! You
know, but first let's...

513
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.000
Um...
Oh, look!

514
00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:05.000
It's a traditional
Freedonian dance.

515
00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:07.000
How amazing does that look?

516
00:34:07.000 --> 00:34:09.000
Say, say, say cheese!

517
00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:12.000
Cheese! I love this.

518
00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:15.000
The little girls go and get the
cheese from the little boys.

519
00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:18.000
That's adorable!

520
00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:24.000
Aw, look at that poor little guy.
With his little boots.

521
00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:26.000
Nobody picked him.

522
00:34:26.000 --> 00:34:28.000
Oh, Margo, why don't
you go up there?

523
00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:29.000
No way!

524
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:30.000
Okay.

525
00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.000
Wait a minute.

526
00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:33.000
No!

527
00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:35.000
Go take a bite of
his cheese, young lady.

528
00:34:35.000 --> 00:34:38.000
Right now!
What?

529
00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:40.000
I'm being tougher, you know?
Like you said.

530
